---
import CapabilityGrid from '../../components/CapabilityGrid.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import ProjectDetailCTA from '../../components/ProjectDetailCTA.astro';
import ProjectDetailHero from '../../components/ProjectDetailHero.astro';
import { aiGatewayCapabilities, aiGatewayDifferentiators } from '../../data/ai-gateway';
---

<Layout
  title="AI Gateway — Conscia Labs"
  description="Governed model access for applications and teams, with policies, routing, usage limits, cost visibility, and hosted MCP tools such as WebSearch. AI Gateway is in closed beta."
  noIndex
>
  <div class="project-page">
    <ProjectDetailHero
      name="AI Gateway"
      category="Artificial Intelligence"
      type="Platform"
      description="One governed route to approved AI models for applications, services, scripts, and developer tools, with organizational access controls, usage limits, and cost visibility."
      lede="Model access with governance built in."
      status="Currently in closed beta. Contact your Conscia representative to learn more."
      externalHref="https://console.ai.conscialabs.com"
    />

    <section class="detail-overview section-light" aria-labelledby="overview-title">
      <div class="container detail-overview__grid">
        <div>
          <p class="section-label">01 / How it works</p>
          <h2 id="overview-title">One controlled route to model access.</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="detail-overview__copy">
          <p>AI Gateway sits between callers and their approved AI models. It applies organizational access policies and limits, selects an eligible model and provider route, and records usage, cost, and audit information.</p>
          <p>OpenAI-style and Anthropic-style APIs let clients integrate with the platform. Supported features and protocol compatibility depend on the enabled model and qualified route; not every provider offers the same capabilities.</p>
          <p>AWS Bedrock is the supported pilot integration. OpenAI, Anthropic Direct, custom OpenAI-compatible endpoints, GitHub Copilot, and Conscia Sovereign AI Cloud adapters are in Preview. The enabled catalog and route qualification determine what a caller can actually use.</p>
          <p>Gateway is infrastructure, not an assistant workspace. Products such as Beacon supply the conversations, context, and working experience around model access.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <CapabilityGrid
      items={aiGatewayCapabilities}
      heading="The infrastructure around a model request."
      introduction="Access, routing, limits, and accountability belong together. Hosted MCP services also provide a separate way for clients to connect to tools such as WebSearch; the inference API does not execute those tools automatically."
    />

    <section class="detail-overview section-light" aria-labelledby="security-engine-title">
      <div class="container detail-overview__grid">
        <div>
          <p class="section-label">03 / Security Suite — Preview</p>
          <h2 id="security-engine-title">Security Enforcement Engine.</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="detail-overview__copy">
          <p>The Security Suite’s separate Security Enforcement Engine is a Preview capability, outside the standard release. Where enabled, it can observe admitted chat input in the background without making inference wait for an inspection result.</p>
          <p>The current preview is observation-only: inspection results do not block requests or change response delivery. Output inspection, enforcement modes, and advanced detection capabilities are not available in this preview.</p>
          <p>The mandatory gateway safeguards and organizational access policies remain separate from this optional observation service.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="differentiators section-light" aria-labelledby="differentiators-title">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="section-intro section-intro--light">
          <div>
            <p class="section-label">04 / What sets it apart</p>
            <h2 id="differentiators-title">A shared layer, with clear responsibilities.</h2>
          </div>
          <p>Developers integrate with model access. Administrators manage the surrounding governance. Downstream products keep ownership of the experience their users work in.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="differentiator-grid">
          {aiGatewayDifferentiators.map((item) => (
            <article class="differentiator" style={`--item-accent: ${item.accent}`}>
              <span class="differentiator__number">{item.number}</span>
              <h3>{item.title}</h3>
              <p>{item.description}</p>
            </article>
          ))}
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="portal-preview section-dark" aria-labelledby="portal-title">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="portal-preview__intro">
          <div>
            <p class="section-label">05 / Developer Portal</p>
            <h2 id="portal-title">From an allowed model to a first request.</h2>
          </div>
          <p>Find models you can access, manage personal keys, try requests in the Sandbox, and follow quickstarts. Usage and limits stay visible alongside the work.</p>
        </div>
        <figure class="portal-preview__figure">
          <img src="/images/ai-gateway/developer-portal.png" alt="AI Gateway Developer Portal showing setup progress, available models, usage, and quickstart actions" loading="lazy" />
          <figcaption>Developer Portal overview</figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>
    </section>

    <ProjectDetailCTA
      label="06 / Closed beta"
      description="AI Gateway is in closed beta. Feature availability varies by enabled service and qualified model route. Contact your Conscia representative to learn more."
      externalHref="https://console.ai.conscialabs.com"
    />
    <Footer />
  </div>
</Layout>
